WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.190
There will be spoilers in this video so make
sure you’ve seen Unbreakable, Split and

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.950
Glass before watching.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.200
If you want to hear my theory about the meaning
behind the clover tattoos, then stick around

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.820
to the end of this video.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.160
Glass begins with four cheerleaders abducted
by Hedwig and David Dunn, who is starting

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.220
to become known as the Overseer, shifting
his focus from petty criminals to The Horde.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.270
We first see him take out these kids who are
filming themselves Superman punching a random

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.480
guy on the street to try to go viral.

00:00:30.499 --> 00:00:34.570
These low criminals are pretending to be superheroes
online, which provides a stark contrast with

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.320
the ending of Glass where real superheroes
leak on social media.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.540
David now has his own security company, Dunn
Home Security.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.180
Elijah says in Unbreakable says that David
works in security for a reason, because he’s

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.490
a born protector, so it makes sense that he
gets his own company.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.850
“You could have been a tax accountant.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.860
You could have owned your own gym.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.860
You could have opened a chain of restaurants.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:58.960
You could have done one of 10,000 things,
but in the end you chose to protect people.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.100
You made that decision, and I find that very,
very interesting.”

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.170
The next day at work, M Night Shyamalan, the
director of the trilogy, makes his cameo appearance,

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.830
and it answers one of the questions I had
going into the movie.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:14.330
He mentions that he’s getting more cameras
because one of his tenants was killed off-site.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:19.480
He’s talking about Dr. Fletcher, so it seems
that Jai, from Split wasn’t just an IT guy

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.930
helping Dr. Fletcher review security footage,
but actually her landlord.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.590
And probably also her landlord.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:29.909
“You can’t use your thumbs to spin the
wheel dumb-***es.”

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:33.960
Jai goes on to see David and he recognises
him as the security guard from those years

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.510
ago, and tells him he used to hang out with
the shady types at the stadium, but he turned

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.510
his life around.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:42.680
This confirms that Stadium Drug Dealer and
Jai are in fact the same character, but this

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.430
is more than just a fun little director’s
cameo, it shows the effect that David had

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.060
cleaning up the crime around his city; he
actually had a positive impact on the community

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.880
and helped turn shady people into functioning
members of society.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.560
David goes out again to look for The Horde
with Joseph giving him tips via headphones

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.960
and GPS tracker.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.630
Not only is this a common superhero trope,
but it’s also a concept that Shyamalan used

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.651
in his 2013 film After Earth, although in
that movie, the roles were reversed and it

00:02:06.651 --> 00:02:08.749
was the father giving advice to his son.

00:02:08.749 --> 00:02:12.290
After David bumps into Hedwig on the street,
he heads toward the brick factory to look

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:16.139
for the girls, and the word Allies is written
in graffiti on a window in the background,

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.160
a foreshadowing the teaming up of Elijah and
The Horde.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.080
“That sounds like the bad guys teaming up."

00:02:24.084 --> 00:02:26.629
In the Unbreakable Things You Missed, I discussed
how upside-down camera composition was used

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:30.599
to foreshadow bad things happening, and the
trend seems to continue in Glass.

00:02:30.599 --> 00:02:33.590
When David first has the confrontation with
The Beast, we see the Beast’s point of view

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.400
as he crawls along the ceiling towards David
and the rescued cheerleaders.

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:46.939
Like many supervillains, The Beast has a signature
move, which is, fittingly, a giant bear hug.

00:02:46.939 --> 00:02:50.939
This is the same attack he used on Dr. Fletcher
during Split, on David during the factory

00:02:50.939 --> 00:02:53.939
fight and the orderly when he and Mr. Glass
are escaping.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:58.469
Throughout the series, broken glass is used
as a metaphor of the well being of the characters,

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:01.749
so when David and The Beast's battle sends
them out of the factory through a shattering

00:03:01.749 --> 00:03:05.790
glass window it spells the beginning of the
end for them, because it leads to their capture

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.389
and placement in Raven Hill Memorial.

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:12.309
Once we arrive at that institution, there
is huge clue about the final twist of the

00:03:12.309 --> 00:03:13.180
movie.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.780
As they are placed in their rooms, we are
shown the point of view of the cameras placed

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.099
around the institution.

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:27.260
The entire movie, these security camera shots
are constantly being shown, the final twist

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.680
is dangled in front of us all along.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.629
The characters are introduced to their new
psychiatrist, Dr. Ellie Staple.

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:36.900
At the end of the movie, we find out that
Dr. Staple is part of the ancient organization

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.970
created to suppress superheroes from the public.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:43.210
She tells Mr. Glass that she they don’t
take sides, she’s not good or evil, she

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.959
essentially falls in the middle.

00:03:44.959 --> 00:03:48.950
In a literal comic book there are staples
placed in the middle crease to hold everything

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:49.950
together.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.909
Her name represents her neutrality.

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:55.430
Casey gets word of The Beast’s capture when
she’s pulled aside at school, and we also

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.969
see that she attended the same school as Joseph
Dunn.

00:03:57.969 --> 00:04:01.450
I’m honestly not entirely sure what the
point of that was outside of furthering the

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.260
idea that everything is connected in a comic
book story, much like how David and Clarence

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.209
W Crumb were on the same train.

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:10.839
Which, as a quick side note, Clarence’s
name continues the theme of alliteration in

00:04:10.839 --> 00:04:15.231
the first two movies with characters like
David Dunn, Casey Cooke, Kevin Crumb, and

00:04:15.231 --> 00:04:16.440
now Clarence Crumb.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.329
There’s also a character that I noticed
in the IMDb credits called Scarlet Shields…

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:23.069
I honestly have no idea who that even is.

00:04:23.069 --> 00:04:27.060
I’m assuming she’s a minor character,
but basically every other minor character

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.610
has a name like Hospital Patient or Cheerleading
Girl #4.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.330
I honestly have no idea who this is supposed
to be.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.650
Maybe she was given a name just to throw off
people trying to look up information online

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.610
before the movie came out, or maybe she’s
given a name because she has an actual name

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.199
tag somewhere in the movie.

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:44.629
Let me know your findings on that in the comments.

00:04:44.629 --> 00:04:49.120
David’s son Joseph meets with Dr. Staple
to try to convince her to let David go free.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.699
When he is unsuccessful, the camera tilts
down into an upside-down position again to

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:54.389
watch Joseph leave the facility.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.680
Just as Joseph saw the original train crash
footage upside-down on the couch in Unbreakable,

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.710
this camera movement in Glass also represents
impending disaster.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:06.409
Speaking of Unbreakable, when I saw the deleted
scene of David coming into a young Joseph’s

00:05:06.409 --> 00:05:11.310
room, I was completely blown away by it, because
somehow I had no idea that these deleted scenes

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.340
from the first film existed, and this one
really works well considering the themes of

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.340
Glass.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.940
Let’s roll it.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.440
“I’m not scared.”

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.240
“That’s great.”

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.020
“You know why?

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.460
I know now.”

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:33.980
“Know what?”

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.940
“Your secret identity.”

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:43.720
So Joseph felt uneasy about the fact that
his father has these incredible abilities

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:48.199
that can’t be explained, but finds comfort
in knowing he has someone to protect him.

00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:51.990
This helps explain why it was so important
for Mr. Glass to outsmart the black clover

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.819
society and broadcast the existence of superheroes
out to the world.

00:05:55.819 --> 00:05:59.669
Next, Casey is given the opportunity to meet
with The Horde, and discovers that her touch

00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:01.820
can bring Kevin forward into the light.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:05.699
My theory as to why Casey has this ability
relates to the fact that the additional identities

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:09.650
were created by Kevin’s brain as a coping
mechanism for the abuse dished out by his

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.650
mother.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.129
It’s stated in Split that the Horde exists
to protect Kevin,

00:06:13.129 --> 00:06:14.900
“Are you in charge?”

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.780
“Yeah, we’ve taken charge.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:19.199
We’re the only ones that can protect Kevin.”

00:06:19.199 --> 00:06:21.099
“We’re all here to protect Kevin.”

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:23.349
“He’s very weak.”

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:28.140
So naturally, the way to bring down these
protections is with love and kindness.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:32.280
Casey is the only one who’s capable of this
because she too has been abused by her Uncle,

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.689
so she knows what kind of gentle hand is needed
to undo the damage.

00:06:35.689 --> 00:06:39.009
When Casey leaves the institution after that,
she puts on the jacket given to her by the

00:06:39.009 --> 00:06:43.280
man working at the Philadelphia Zoo who escorts
her out of danger at the end of Split.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:47.060
My guess is that she still wears that jacket
as a reminder of how she stood up to The Beast

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:51.159
-- something that also gave her the strength
to stand up to her Uncle, and just to be a

00:06:51.159 --> 00:06:52.979
stronger, braver person overall.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:57.360
In the final examination scene, Dr. Staple
tries to convince Mr. Glass, The Horde and

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.469
The Overseer that they don’t actually have
super powers by giving rational explanations

00:07:01.469 --> 00:07:05.319
for everything that has happened and telling
them they will remain institutionalized for

00:07:05.319 --> 00:07:08.879
the rest of their lives if they are unable
to overcome their “disorder”.

00:07:08.879 --> 00:07:12.699
In a way, she is actually telling the truth
-- although we don’t know it yet, the black

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:17.069
clover society was planning to kill them if
Dr. Staple didn’t successfully convince

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.330
them they are ordinary in the three day timespan.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.650
But I’ll get back to the black clover society
later in this video.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:27.319
Dr. Staple tells David he has symptoms of
the supposed superhero disorder, but lacks

00:07:27.319 --> 00:07:30.949
some kind of anchoring incident that made
him realize that he is a superhero, which

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:35.349
is funny because the “anchoring incident”
he thinks of is literally him drowning like

00:07:35.349 --> 00:07:36.349
an anchor.

00:07:36.349 --> 00:07:39.629
One of the main talking points that Dr. Staple
uses to try to convince them that they are

00:07:39.629 --> 00:07:43.909
ordinary, is that if superheroes do exist,
why would there only be the three of them?

00:07:43.909 --> 00:07:48.469
This is Dr. Staple counting on the fact that
her black clover society will always be successful

00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:50.919
in suppressing any supers from the public
eye.

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:54.560
David and Patricia appear to have their faith
in their own powers shaken.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.449
Elijah, doesn’t respond, because he’s
pretending to be a vegetable, but he knows

00:07:58.449 --> 00:08:00.640
that Dr. Staple is lying to them.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:10.900
All the talk of comic books sends Casey to
the comic-book store to do some of her own

00:08:10.909 --> 00:08:15.159
research, and the store is owned by none other
than the comic book store clerk from Unbreakable.

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:19.490
It seems that his suspicious of pervs in back
of the store hasn’t changed either, when

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:23.919
he yells to Joseph, “you better not be one
of those Hello Kitty pervs.”

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:30.230
“You better not be jacking off to the Japanese
comics I swear to God.”

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.759
--
Just as the mirror reflection shots are used

00:08:31.759 --> 00:08:36.160
to introduce villains in Unbreakable and Split,
similar shots are used in Glass to show that

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.790
something is not right.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:42.280
David sits on floor of his cell and his reflection
is distorted by the curved wall.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:45.650
Across the way, The Horde is seen in a distorted
reflection through a curved mirror.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:49.731
It is shortly after this that we discover
Elijah was faking his sedation and has the

00:08:49.731 --> 00:08:54.420
ability to sneak out of his room and he discovers
the magazine advertising the opening of Osaka

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:55.420
Tower.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:59.280
Just as the previous movies had subtle references
to The Fantastic Four and Teen Titans, the

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.160
headline of this article calls Osaka Tower
a true MARVEL.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.280
Elijah tells The Beast that his plan is to
attack the tower on its opening date, December

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.790
7th, which is Pearl Harbor Day another major
American disaster.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:15.460
More importantly, that’s also my birthday,
so put that down in your calendar right now.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.320
Right now.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:22.080
Then we get a glimpse into Elijah’s past,
when he sneaks onto a carnival ride and tries

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.780
to protect himself using stuffed animals.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:26.540
This is another deleted scene, but again,
it works really well here because The Beast

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.710
ends protecting him from the orderlies and
the police as they break out of the hospital,

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:34.040
so it’s kind of as if he’s been protected
by animals every step of the way.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.890
It’s also interesting to note that his plan
on the carnival ride backfires, and he ends

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.770
up breaking his shoulder, just as The Beast
turns on him at the end of Glass and breaks

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.690
his shoulder, an injury he would never overcome.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:48.340
After Elijah discovers the powers of The Beast,
he formulates his plan to have The Beast battle

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:49.490
David in front of the world.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:53.340
I think it’s important to note that it was
never Mr. Glass’s real intention to go to

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:56.690
the tower, all he really needed to do was
convince The Beast to break them out so he

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:57.720
could stream it using the cameras.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:03.240
Can we copystrike Mr Glass's latest video?

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.380
And for anyone who felt that David Dunn’s
part in all of this was a little underwhelming,

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:10.220
let’s not forget that it was most likely
Dunn’s security company who provided all

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:13.140
the cameras to the institution in the first
place.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.790
Part of Elijah’s plan was to change out
the lens of the machine used for his surgery,

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:20.620
then get himself caught lollygagging around
on camera so that the doctor moves up the

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:21.880
date of his operation.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:26.270
This is important because it allows the orderly,
Daryl, to let his guard down around Elijah,

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:29.810
giving him the opportunity to slit his throat
with the broken shard of glass.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:34.700
And just as Elijah’s broken glass cane represented
his injuries in Unbreakable, the broken picture

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.780
frames foreshadow his eventual demise in Glass.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.650
All three characters have their “broken
glass moment”.

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:44.650
At the end of the second act there are a couple
more clever uses of shots that use mirror

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:45.690
reflections to tell us something.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:49.470
The first is Dr. Staple getting out of her
car and heading into Raven Hill Memorial,

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.090
which we see through her side mirror.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:55.190
These mirrors always come with a disclaimer:
objects in mirror are closer than they appear.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:59.240
Well, Dr. Staple is not just a psychiatrist
as she appears to be, because she’s actually

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:01.130
part of this secret organization.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:04.880
Our earlier mirror shots of David and The
Horde are distorted by curved mirrors, but

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:08.830
when Elijah finally meets The Beast, he first
sees the transformation through the reflection

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.370
of a glass cabinet.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.420
There’s no distortion here, which tells
us that things are going to be essentially

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:16.830
as they should be with the impending clash
of good vs. evil.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:21.390
Then Dr. Staple realizes that Elijah has broken
out, she sees the news report on TV about

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:25.330
the opening of Osaka Tower, and thinks Mr.
Glass is going to sabotage it.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.140
Also, the reporter is the same guy who reports
on the missing girls in Split, and on the

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:31.780
news ticker at the bottom, there is a report
about cryptocurrency.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:36.420
Krypton is the name of Superman’s home planet,
and Superman is referenced several times throughout

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.420
Glass.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:41.270
Shortly after, the final battle begins, and
Dr. Staple curiously tells someone to make

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:44.490
sure to keep patients and staff away from
the south side windows.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.550
This is because she knows that David, Elijah
and Kevin’s powers are real, and it’s

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:50.790
her duty to make sure nobody finds out about
them.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:53.930
So that brings us back to this whole black
clover society.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:54.960
Who are they?

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:56.200
Where did they come from?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.350
Why do they have these matching tattoos?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:01.260
And what do they have to do with Split and
Unbreakable?

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:03.800
All of the answers to all of these questions are
coming up.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:12.620
At the end of the confrontation, a mysterious
group of SWAT members all sharing a wrist

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:16.870
tattoo of black three leaf clover show up
to kill David and The Beast.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:19.600
Dr. Staple is revealed to be a part of this
society.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.490
She explains that they are a group that has
been around for 10,000 years to keep superheroes

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:27.730
out of the public eye, because it’s not
fair to the rest of society to have Gods walking

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:28.730
among us.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:32.550
Dr. Staple’s mission the entire time was
to get them to believe that their powers weren’t

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:35.100
real so they can go on living ordinary lives.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:39.190
She was given the three days to do so, but
if she failed, the alternative was some kind

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.160
of brain surgery, or death.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:45.930
In Split, we are shown how the organization’s
manipulation of society has worked.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:50.110
Society sees The Horde’s dissociative identity
disorder as a problem, a mental illness that

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.110
needs to be cured.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:55.550
Dr. Fletcher’s thesis to the medical community
is that maybe those with this condition are

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.080
actually extraordinarily gifted.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:04.210
“Well, we look at people who have been shattered
and different as less than.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:09.060
What if they are more than us?”

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:13.740
But Dr. Fletcher is largely rejected by her
peers, and it’s because the black clover

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:18.480
society has been working for 10,000 years
to condition us to see this as a mental illness.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:23.210
That’s exactly what Dr. Staple does in Glass,
she rounds up three of the most extraordinary

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:27.430
supers in Philadelphia and tries to convince
them that something is wrong with them and

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:28.430
that they need treatment.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:32.220
That’s why she wants Casey to get Kevin
to hold onto the light, because she is aware

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:35.000
of the power someone with DID is capable of.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.840
The existence of this group also explains
a question brought up way back when Elijah

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.260
and David have their first meeting in Unbreakable.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:47.120
“I believe comics are our last link to an
ancient way of passing on history.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.890
The Egyptians drew on walls.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:53.940
Countries all over the world still pass on
knowledge through pictorial forms.”

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:57.820
Remember when Dr. Staple is meeting with Joseph,
Casey and Elijah’s mother, and tries to

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:00.380
convince them that comics are nothing more
than fantasy?

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:03.580
She even brings up comic-book conventions
to try to invalidate them.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:07.500
The only time she gets frustrated is when
they try to link their situation to what they

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.600
have seen in comic books.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:12.780
The clover society is there to ensure that these
stories exist through pictures, as seemingly

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.570
fictional stories, but nothing more.

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:20.290
“I believe comics are a form of history
that someone somewhere felt or experienced.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:24.910
Then of course those experiences and that
history got chewed up in the commercial machine,

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:28.990
got jazzed up, made into titillating cartoons
for the sale rack.”

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:34.080
In Glass, the “someone somewhere” Elijah
is referring to is his mother, Joseph and

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:38.200
Casey, only this time instead of distributing
comics to be chewed up in the commercial machine,

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.850
they have actual video evidence of the existence
of these powers.

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:46.450
Dr. Staple also mentions that when one super
appears, another is likely to appear opposite

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:50.300
of him, and it just leads to conflict, which
is why she feels the clover society needs

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.770
to appear to pacify them.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:57.080
“If there is someone like me in the world
and I am at one end of the spectrum, couldn’t

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.900
there be someone else opposite of me at the
other end.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:06.140
Someone who doesn’t get sick, who doesn’t
get hurt like the rest of us.

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:09.560
And he probably doesn’t even know it.”

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:13.680
OK, but why the black clover tattoos, that
seems kind of random?

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.680
Well maybe not.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.720
We can look at it from the secret organization’s
perspective and from a filmmaking perspective.

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:21.350
First from a filmmaking perspective.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:25.500
The fact that David, Elijah and The Horde’s
journey as superpowered humans ends with a

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:28.160
tattoo of these clovers kind of brings the
trilogy full circle.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.620
Let’s go wayyy back to when we are introduced
to David in Unbreakable.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:36.250
A woman appears asking him if he’s alone,
and she takes the spot next to him on the

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.250
train.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:40.940
He notices a tattoo on her abdomen which appears
to be a rose, but we only see the bottom of

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.800
the stem because this is the very root of
David’s story.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:47.220
When we see the secret society’s clover
tattoos at the very end of David’s story,

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:51.180
we’re seeing the top of the plant, so it's
as if we’ve come all the way around.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:54.390
But then why not use a rose tattoo for the
society as well?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.580
The clover does a better job of representing
their values.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:16:00.930
They essentially want to purge the world of
anyone who has these rare, special powers.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.130
A four leaf clover is considered a rare and
lucky find, much like how a superhero is a

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.980
rare incredible standout in our society.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:11.610
But the black clover people don’t want that,
they want everyone to be a three leaf clover

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.510
and that’s why is was chosen as the symbol
of their organization.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:18.460
Finally, there was one other minute detail
that I felt really brought the series to a

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.720
nice conclusion.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:23.090
Mr. Glass famously gets his supervillain name
from the kids that made fun of his condition,

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:24.860
osteogenesis imperfecta.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.280
They called me Mr. Glass.”

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:31.790
Elijah’s mother lives across from a playground,
we see this in a flashback during Unbreakable.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.440
At the end of Glass, before the email comes
in from Elijah containing the footage of the

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:39.000
final battle, you can hear the sounds of children
playing from outside.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:43.400
How fitting that the very playground that the kids
that poked fun of Elijah at, part of what put

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:47.870
the villain idea in his head in the first place and gave him
his awakening as a supervillain can be heard

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:52.090
again, just before Elijah’s mother puts
out that video to help all heroes and villains

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:55.320
across the world have their realization and
awakening.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:59.300
When David first accepts his newfound powers
in Unbreakable, Elijah tells him to go to

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:01.700
where there are people, and he goes to the
train station.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:06.530
That’s exactly what Mrs. Price, Joseph and
Casey do when they unveil the existence of

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:13.560
these comic book heroes to the world.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.180
If you enjoyed this video, you can check out
my Things You Missed episodes on Unbreakable

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:23.170
and Split as well, and make sure you subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:28.870
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:30.309
Assuming, we both survive.

